- 08: Sign In → 01_Home, Register Now → 07_Sign_Up, Forgot Password? → 09_Forgot_Password\n- 09: Send Confirmation Code → 10_Confirmation_Code, Login → 08_Sign_In\n- 10: Recover Account → 11_New_Password\n- 11: Submit → 01_Home\n\n**Fixed copy:**\n- Home copy:\n  - Deals Of The Month: \"Hand-picked styles at their best prices this month — once the timer runs out, the deals are gone.\"\n  - New Arrivals: \"Fresh pieces just landed: easy dresses, cosy knits and everyday shirts for the new season.\"\n  - Instagram: \"Tag @fasco to be featured — real outfits from our community, styled your way.\"\n  - Testimonials: \"Real reviews from people who shop with FASCO.\"\n  - Newsletter: \"Be the first to hear about new arrivals, exclusive deals and styling tips. No spam — unsubscribe anytime.\"\n- Collection banner: \"Men Collection · Classic Gentleman\", labels Flat Cap · Cotton Shirt · Suspender · Leather Shoes, DESCRIPTION: \"A sharp, vintage-inspired look built around a wool flat cap, a crisp cotton shirt and classic suspenders. Easy to dress up or down, and made to last for years.\" Size: M · $100.00 · Buy Now\n- New Arrivals cards: Shiny Dress, Long Dress, Full Sweater, White Dress, Colorful Dress, White Shirt — each FASCO · 5-star · (4.1k) Customer Reviews · $95.50 · Almost Sold Out\n- Testimonials: Suzan B. · UI Designer, James K. · Traveler (current), Megen W. · UI Designer with quotes\n- People Also Loved: \"Shoppers who looked at this jacket also loved these deals — grab them before the timer runs out.\"\n- Shop products: Rounded Red Hat $8.00, Linen-blend Shirt $17.00 Sold Out, Long-sleeve Coat $106.00, Boxy Denim Hat $25.00, Linen Plain Top $25.00, Oversized T-shirt $11.00 old $14.00, Polarised Sunglasses $18.00 old $21.00, Rockstar Jacket $22.00, Dotted Black Dress $20.00\n- Denim Jacket: FASCO · (3) reviews · $39.00 · old $59.00 · Save 33% · sizes M L XL XXL (M selected) · Colors Blue Black Lilac (Blue selected) · Quantity 1 · 24 people viewing · 00:05:59:47 · Only 9 left · Jul 30 - Aug 03 · over $75\n- Cart: Subtotal $39.00, Buy $36.00 more..., Checkout: Subtotal $39.00 Shipping $40.00 Total $79.00\n- Features: High Quality · crafted from top materials (Trophy), Warranty Protection · Over 2 years (Guarantee), Free Shipping · Order over $75 (Shipping), 24 / 7 Support · Dedicated support (Support)\n\nNow I need to look at the component details — the Button (1:24) and Text Field (1:27) symbols. Let me get design context for those, and also look at a couple of the media symbols to understand their structure. Let me get design context on 1:5 (Foundations), 1:20 (Components), and 6:81 (Media) to see actual fills, fonts, etc.\n\nActually, get_design_context returns detailed XML with properties. Let me call it on the components frame 1:20 to see the Button and Text Field details. And maybe on 6:85 to see photo symbol structure.\n\nThe plan for building:\n\nGiven the scale (11 frames, 1920 wide, some very tall like home ~ maybe 8000px), this is a huge job. I'll need to be efficient with use_figma calls. Strategy:\n\n1. First, set up the workspace: load fonts (Volkhov Regular/Bold/Italic, Poppins Regular/Medium/SemiBold), copy media components into workspace page (or create my own components). The brief says \"Use the photos, the avatars, the sign-in logos and the icons from 04 · Media.\" and media page says \"Copy these components into your own file and use them as instances.\"\n\nActually the media symbols are components (symbol nodes) in this file. Since I'm working in the same file, I can create instances of them directly via `figma.createComponentFromNode` or `comp.createInstance()`. The nodes are component nodes — id like 6:32 (Photo_Collection symbol). I can use `figma.getNodeById(\"6:32\")` and check if it's a ComponentNode, then `.createInstance()`.\n\n2. Create my own local components in the workspace: Header (home + store variants), Footer (home + store variants), Product Card (new arrivals + shop variants), Feature strip, Section heading, Newsletter, Instagram strip, Collection banner, Deal slider, Testimonial card, etc. But given the complexity, building components for everything might take too many API calls. The brief says \"Design all other states, the header, the footer, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file.\" — I should create key components: Header variants, Footer variants, Product Card, etc. But I need to balance effort. Let me create components for the most reused things:\n   - Store Header (with variant for current nav item) — used on 02-06\n   - Home Header — used on 01\n   - Store Footer — 02-06\n   - Home Footer — 01\n   - Newsletter block — 01, 02, 03, 05, 06 (5 uses)\n   - Collection banner — 01, 02, 03\n   - Features strip — 01, 02, 03\n   - Instagram strip — 01, 02\n   - Product card (new arrivals) — 01 (6x)\n   - Shop product card — 02 (9x)\n   - Deal slider block — 01, 03\n   - Button/Text Field — reuse given ones (1:24, 1:27)\n\nTo be efficient, I'll create components, then instances. But since each use_figma call has 50k char limit, I'll break into many calls.\n\nAlso there's an important note: \"IMPORTANT: After you call this tool, you MUST call get_design_context if trying to implement the design\". I should call get_design_context on key nodes to understand their structure: 1:20 (components), maybe 1:9 (brand colors), 6:85. Let me call get_design_context on 1:20 first to see Button/Text Field internals.\n\nPlan of use_figma calls:\n1. Setup: load fonts, check component availability, create base color styles maybe. Copy Button/Text Field into workspace as my components (or instance them from the original components — they're in the reference page; creating instances directly references the same component, which is fine and even desired: \"Reuse the components in 02 · Components\").\n\nActually wait — \"Reuse the components in 02 · Components\" — the Button and Text Field are components in the file, so I can create