(gold)\n- Success/stock: #2E7D4F\n- Link: #000000 underlined\n\nSpacing: 8px base. Section padding 96 top/bottom.\n\nLet me define the page grid: 1400px container, 24px gutters.\n\nHome page layout (01_Home):\n1. Home header (height 96): FASCO wordmark (Volkhov Bold 32), nav center (Home current, Deals, New Arrivals, Packages), right: Sign in (text), Sign Up (button instance)\n2. Hero collage: photos Photo_Hero_Left (156×220 scaled), Photo_Hero_Top (333×220), Photo_Hero_Bottom (147×220), Photo_Hero_Right (147×220) arranged around center text \"ULTIMATE\" / \"SALE\" / \"NEW COLLECTION\" / SHOP NOW button. Classic FASCO layout: left column small photo bottom-left, big top photo, right photo, center headline. I'll design: center text block with \"ULTIMATE\" (Volkhov), \"SALE\" big, \"NEW COLLECTION\" letter-spaced, SHOP NOW button. Photos: Left photo at left side mid, Top photo upper-right area, Bottom photo lower-left, Right photo right-mid. \n3. Brands strip: 5 wordmarks (Minimog, Retrolie, Brook, Learts, Vagabond) — text in a distinct font style (Poppins SemiBold, maybe uppercase, gray)\n4. Collection banner (shared component): Photo_Collection as background right side, content: \"Men Collection\" label, \"Classic Gentleman\" heading, item labels row (Flat Cap · Cotton Shirt · Suspender · Leather Shoes), DESCRIPTION + copy, \"Size: M\", \"$100.00\", \"Buy Now\" button\n5. Deals Of The Month: left deal slides (Photo_Deal_1/2/3 stacked or one big?), per brief: \"deal slides Photo_Deal_1, Photo_Deal_2, Photo_Deal_3 · current slide card '01 — Spring Sale' · '30% OFF' · previous/next · slide indicator: 4 slides, current 1\". Design: left column heading + copy + countdown (02 Days 06 Hr 05 Mins 30 Sec) + Buy Now + slide indicator; right: big photo (Photo_Deal_1) with overlaid card \"01 — Spring Sale\" \"30% OFF\", arrows. Hmm, but \"deal slides Photo_Deal_1, Photo_Deal_2, Photo_Deal_3\" — could show a row of 3 photos. I'll show the three photos as the slide area: maybe a large left photo (Deal_1) and two stacked right (Deal_2, Deal_3)? Simpler: one row with three photos, and the \"current slide card\" overlay on the first. Plus arrows and \"01 / 04\" indicator.\n6. Features strip (shared): 4 items with icon, title, line, separated by vertical lines\n7. New Arrivals: heading, copy, tabs (Men's Fashion current? no — current: Women's Fashion), 6 product cards in grid (3 cols × 2 rows), each card: photo, brand FASCO, name, 5 stars, (4.1k) Customer Reviews, $95.50, \"Almost Sold Out\" badge. View More button → 02_Shop.\n8. Newsletter: Photo_Subscribe_Left and Photo_Subscribe_Right flanking, heading \"Subscribe To Our Newsletter\", copy, email field + \"Subscribe Now\" button\n9. Testimonials: heading \"This Is What Our Customers Say\", copy, 3 cards (avatar, quote, 5 stars, name, role), current James K. (highlighted), prev/next arrows\n10. Instagram: heading \"Follow Us On Instagram\", copy, 7 photos row (mixed heights? maybe uniform squares) — the photos have varied native widths (147, 143, 220, 147, 330, 330, 330). I can crop freely. I'll make a 7-photo strip with equal display size, e.g., 188×240 each... Total width 1400: 7 photos with 16 gaps: (1400 - 6*16)/7 = 184.86 each. I'll resize instances to ~184×230. Or use varied sizes like masonry. Simplest: uniform 184×232.\n11. Home footer: big FASCO wordmark, links Support Center, Invoicing, Contract, Careers, Blog, FAQs, copyright line.\n\nStore pages 02–06 share: Store header, collection banner (02,03), features (02,03), newsletter, instagram (02 only), store footer.\n\n02_Shop: title \"Fashion\" + breadcrumb Home › Fashion; toolbar (sort \"Best selling\" with chevron down, view grid/list icons, current grid); left filters sidebar (Filters; Size S M L XL; Colors swatches; Prices $0-$50 etc; Brands Minimog, Retrolie, Brook, Learts, Vagabond, Abby; Collections All products, Best sellers, New arrivals, Accessories; Tags Fashion, Hats, Sandal, Belt, Bags, Sneaker, Denim, Sunglasses, Beachwear); right: 9 product cards 3×3 grid (name, price, old price where given, Sold Out badge on Linen-blend Shirt); pagination 1 2 3 next, current 1.\n\n03_Product: breadcrumb maybe (not required). Gallery left: main Photo_Denim_Jacket_Blue_2 (scaled ~520×700?) + thumbnails row of 6 (Lilac, Blue_1, Blue_2, Blue_3, Black_1, Black_2). Right: brand FASCO, \"Denim Jacket\" title, rating stars + (3), $39.00 + old $59.00 + Save 33% badge; urgency: Icon_Eye \"24 people are viewing this right now\", \"Hurry up! Sale ends in:\" 00 : 05 : 59 : 47 (countdown boxes), \"Only 9 item(s) left in stock!\" + stock level bar; Options: \"Size: M\" M L XL XXL (M selected), \"Color: Blue\" Blue Black Lilac (Blue selected — swatches with labels); Quantity − 1 +; \"Add to cart\" button; actions row: Compare, Ask a question, Share (with icons); delivery: \"Estimated Delivery:\" Jul 30 - Aug 03 (Icon_Delivery), \"Free Shipping & Returns:\" On all orders over $75 (Icon_Returns), \"Guarantee safe & secure checkout\"; People Also Loved section below with countdown and deal slides like Deals Of The Month.\n\n04_Mini_Cart: full 1920×1080-ish frame: background = simplified product page snapshot (I can instance the product page frame scaled down? That's heavy. Alternative: place a scaled instance of the 03_Product frame inside — actually in Figma I can instance a frame? No, frames can't be instanced directly, but I can clone the frame node and scale it. Cloning the whole product page as the backdrop is allowed since it's in the same file. I could use `figma.getNodeById(productFrameId).clone()`, set width scale... Frames don't scale content automatically; I'd need rescale() — there's `node.rescale(scale)` on some nodes? Plugin API: `rescale` exists on nodes? There's `figma.flatten`... Actually `node.rescale(scale)` is available on `RectangleNode`? Hmm. There is `rescale` on `TextNode`? Let me recall: The Plugin API has `node.rescale(scale)` for... I believe `rescale()` is a method on `VectorNode`? No — I recall `rescale` exists on most node types via `LayoutMixin`? Checking memory: LayoutMixin has `resize`, `resizeWithoutConstraints`, `rescale`? I'm fairly confident `rescale(scale: number)` IS part of LayoutMixin in the plugin API (added a while ago). Yes — LayoutMixin.rescale(scale) exists. So I can clone product frame and rescale to fit backdrop. But cloned content = huge duplicate. It's acceptable in Figma (it's a snapshot). But it would make file heavy and screenshot complex. Alternative: simplified backdrop — dim overlay over a lightly-simulated product page (header + simplified content). The brief: \"Behind the drawer: the 03_Product page, inactive; header cart shows count 1\". For fidelity, cloning is the best. Let me try clone + rescale. If rescale fails, fallback: place clone at scale 1 with overlay (frame is 1920 wide anyway; heights equal). Then add dim overlay + drawer on right side.\n\nActually simpler: build 04_Mini_Cart as 1920×(product height) frame; clone 03_Product frame contents into it (clone node, append, position 0,0), then overlay a scrim rectangle (rgba(0,0,0,0.5)) and the drawer on the right (~420 wide, white, full height). Header cart count 1 — the cloned header would show count 0 (I'll build the product header cart without count... but brief says on 04 header cart shows count 1). Hmm — the mini cart backdrop should show count 1. Option: after cloning, find the cart badge in the clone and set to \"1\". Doable: name the badge text uniquely (\"CartCount\") and search clone children. I'll do that.\n\n05_Cart: store header (cart count 1), title \"Shopping Cart\", breadcrumb Home › Your Shopping Cart, cart table (Product | Price | Quantity | Total) with row (photo thumb, Denim Jacket, Color : Blue, Remove, $39.00, stepper −01+, $39.00), gift wrap checkbox, Subtotal $39.00, Checkout button. Newsletter + footer.\n\n06_Checkout: store header (count 1), title \"FASCO Checkout\", left column: Contact (Don't have an account? Create Account; Email Address), Delivery (Country/Region dropdown, First Name, Last Name, Address, City, Postal Code, Save This Info checkbox), Payment (Credit Card, Card Number with lock icon, Expiration Date, Security Code, Card Holder Name, checkbox, Pay Now button). Right: order summary (product thumb ×1, Denim Jacket, Blue, $39.00; Discount code + Apply; Subtotal $39.00, Shipping $40.00, Total $79.00).\n\n07–11: full-screen 1920×1080 sign-in pages: left media photo, right card. Card: FASCO wordmark top, form, social buttons, \"FASCO Terms & Conditions\" at bottom. Design: split layout — left half photo (Photo_Sign_In / Photo_Sign_Up enlarged), right half white with centered card.\n\nOrder of building (to enable cloning for 04): build components → 01_Home → 02_Shop → 03_Product → 04_Mini_Cart (clone product) → 05_Cart → 06_Checkout → 07..11 → prototype wiring → screenshots.\n\nPrototype wiring: use `figma.currentPage`... For links, `frameId` on nodes: set `node.prototypeStartPoint`? In plugin API: create interactions via `node.prototypeStartPoint = ...`? The API: `prototypeStartPoint`/`prototypeRestartStartPoint` are on... Actually interactions are set via `node.prototypeInteractions`? Hmm, not directly settable historically. The supported way: `node.prototypeStartPoint = { type: 'NODE', nodeId: ... }`? Let me think. In the Figma Plugin API, `PrototypeAttachMixin`? There is `componentNode.prototypeStartPoint` for flow starting points. For interactions: nodes have `reactions` property: `node.reactions = [{ action: { type: 'NODE', destinationId: '123:456' }, trigger: { type: 'ON_CLICK' } }]`. Yes! `reactions` is settable: each reaction = { action: {type: \"NODE\", destinationId, navigation?: \"NAVIGATE\", transition...}, trigger: {type: \"ON_CLICK\"} }. That's the way. I'll set reactions on the buttons.\n\nNote: reactions can be set on nodes inside frames. Good.\n\nMedia instancing: photo components are COMPONENT nodes (symbol). To instance: `const comp = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"6:32\"); comp.createInstance()`. In plugin API within use_figma, getNodeById is sync `figma.getNodeById(id)` (deprecated but works) or `await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id)`. I'll use getNodeByIdAsync.\n\nFor photos, instances of 220×220 or 330×220 — I'll resize instances to my grid (resizing instance is fine).\n\nFonts: need to load Volkhov (styles: Regular, Bold, Italic maybe) and Poppins (Regular, Medium, SemiBold, Bold). Use `figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Volkhov\", style:\"Regular\"})` etc. If a style is missing it throws — I'll try/catch and report. Common Google Fonts in Figma: Volkhov has Regular, Italic, Bold, Bold Italic. Poppins has Thin..Black + italics.\n\nLet me now fetch design context for the Components frame (1:20) to see the exact Button and Text Field structure (fills, radii, text). Also the Foundations (1:5) maybe for type samples. And I might want a screenshot of the media page later. Let me get design context for 1:20 and 6:81 might be too big; skip media details, instance them anyway.\n\nLet me call get_design_context on 1:20.","signature":"a3bce4ffe99e486595fc6c92"}],"id":"785de6b7-3dfc-4de2-b473-99f5b89555d1","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"115d8fd2-329d-45e7-8005-49ec3e8a31e3","uuid":"22094776-39ba-4451-83cf-9754d83917c5","timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:03:40.159Z","thinking_duration_ms":103316}
