 rc.cornerRadius=r; if(stroke){rc.strokes=[F(stroke)]; rc.strokeWeight=sw;} if(name) rc.name=name; parent.appendChild(rc); return rc; }\nasync function inst(id, parent, x, y, w, h, name) { const c = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id); const i = c.createInstance(); parent.appendChild(i); i.x=x; i.y=y; if(w&&h) i.resize(w,h); else if(w) i.rescale(w/i.width); if(name) i.name=name||i.name; return i; }\n```\n\nWait — resize on instance: allowed (overrides). For photos keeping aspect: I'll set both w and h as computed.\n\nAlso `rescale` exists on instances? LayoutMixin.rescale(scale) — yes it exists generally. I'll mostly use resize with explicit dims.\n\nSetting icon colors inside instance: `i.findOne(n=>n.type===\"VECTOR\").fills=[F(hex)]` — instances allow fill overrides on children. Stars: 6:37 inner vector; for gold stars override fills.\n\nText override in instance: `i.findOne(n=>n.type===\"TEXT\" && n.name===\"X\").characters = \"...\"` — allowed if font loaded.\n\nComponent creation: `const comp = figma.createComponent(); comp.resizeWithoutConstraints(w,h); ...` then add children into comp. To instance: `comp.createInstance()`.\n\nI should also set `comp.description`. Not necessary.\n\nOne concern: creating components on the Workspace page then frames referencing them — fine.\n\nCart count badge in Store Header: text node named \"CartCount\" — default \"0\"? On 03-04 need count 1? Brief: \"the cart shows count 1 on 04–06\" and 02 header no count mention (\"cart (Icon_Cart)\") — 02 no count; 03 no count mention (header listed without count; but 04 must show count 1 in header cart); 05, 06 count 1. So default header: no badge. Instances on 05, 06, and clone for 04 show badge with \"1\". I'll add badge child with visible=false default; override visible=true and text \"1\" where needed.\n\nStore header \"current\" nav item: Home/Shop/Products/Pages; current Shop on 02, Products on 03–04, none on 05–06. How to show current: black pill behind item or black text vs gray. I