ice.\n4. SoldOutOverlay hidden → missing. INVERT: visible in component → hide on non-sold-out cards.\n\nBut wait — modifying the MAIN components affects the component definitions (fine, they're my components). But does changing visibility in the main component propagate to EXISTING instances? Yes, unless overridden. Since no instance has overrides for those (they're missing entirely), changing main component → all instances update.\n\nHowever — the check in the failed 02_Shop: partialShop = null?! \"02_Shop\" frame not found and shopChildren 0. So the failed call apparently did NOT persist the frame? Interesting — maybe the whole use_figma call is transactional: on error, rollback! That's great news: failed calls leave no partial state. (01_Home rebuild after error: I removed old — wait, in that rebuild I did `const old=ws.findOne(n=>n.name===\"01_Home\");if(old)old.remove();` and it found nothing? Actually the first failed 01_Home call also left no frame due to rollback — consistent.)\n\nSo: failed calls roll back. \n\nPlan:\n1. Fix components (invert hidden→visible for: checkbox Check, headerStore CartBadge+CartCount, cardShop OldPrice + SoldOutOverlay).\n   - But careful: cart badge visible in headerStore main → instances on 02_Shop/03_Product would show \"1\" — brief says cart count 1 only on 04–06. I'll hide per instance on 02/03 (override allowed since node now exists in instance).\n2. Re-run 02_Shop with corrected logic:\n   - Price checks: all unchecked → set Check visible=false for all 5 (they'll be visible from component). Or keep first checked as planned.\n   - SoldOutOverlay: set visible=false on all 8 non-sold-out cards; true on Linen-blend Shirt.\n   - OldPrice: visible=false on 7 cards; true+reposition on 6,7.\n\nAlso note: instance child overrides — setting visible=false on instance children works.\n\nAlso for cardArrival — Status etc all visible, fine.\n\nDealSlider Bar1-3: visible ✓. Nothing hidden there.\n\nTestimonial component — not used in 01 (