{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"02_Shop built: 24:278, 95 children. Log shows one MISS: after setting SoldOutOverlay visible=false (an override), setting it back to visible=true fails — because once overridden to hidden... it gets stripped? Interesting: setting visible=false on the instance child REMOVES it (strips), so subsequent findOne fails. That explains earlier failures too? Earlier failing run: cards set `SoldOutOverlay visible=false` first — fine; then for sold card set true → MISS → null → error. Yes! That's exactly the earlier failure: `ci.findOne(...).visible=false` succeeded, then `if(sold) ci.findOne(...).visible=true` → null.\n\nRule learned: **instance-child visibility can be set ONCE (from visible→hidden); can't toggle back (node disappears on hide)**. Actually more precisely: setting hidden strips the node; the override can't be undone in-session. So: never hide then re-show; hide only things not needed later. For the sold-out card (k=1) I must NOT hide its overlay first.\n\nFix for card1: rebuild just that card's overlay at frame level (dim + pill), since the instance's overlay was hidden. Add: dim rect 340×340 white 55% at (960,290)…wait card k=1 at x=960,y=290. Add dim + pill + \"Sold Out\" text at frame level on top. Also ensure it's above the card (appendChild → top, but PhotoCover for card1 was appended after card — order: card, PhotoCover, then overlays appended later are on top ✓).\n\nAdd now in a small fix call. Then continue with 03_Product.\n\nAlso note for future frames: for any node I need visible on SOME instances, don't hide-then-show; instead hide on the instances that don't need it (each instance child hidden once = fine) and leave the ones needing it untouched. E.g., header cart badge: hide on 02, 03 (backdrop clone for 04 needs badge VISIBLE — it's a clone of 03's frame... the clone will have badge hidden because 03's instance had it hidden with override! Override bakes into clone. So on the 04 backdrop clone, I need badge visible again — CAN'T un-hide. Workaround: build the badge separately on the backdrop clone (new ellipse + text at frame level) — easy since it's just a black dot + \"1\".\n\nOK. Fix card1 overlay now, then build 03_Product.","signature":"ec8b9b45ac474c1396c6e71a"}],"id":"8820c4d7-431e-46ab-8f14-ba2692ff5365","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"115d8fd2-329d-45e7-8005-49ec3e8a31e3","uuid":"4de94ae0-40b0-4e7b-9cc5-72d1eb57831a","timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:27:55.198Z","thinking_duration_ms":14255}
