{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"05_Cart done (27:675). Next 06_Checkout @ (11000,0): headerStore badge visible; \"FASCO Checkout\" Volkhov 44; left col: Contact (Email Address field 1:27), Delivery (Country/Region dropdown row + 6:17, First Name/Last Name, Address, City + Postal Code, \"Save This Information\" checkbox checked), Payment (Credit Card selected radio, Card Number field + Lock 6:29, Expiration + Security Code, Card Holder, checkbox, Pay Now button no link); right col order summary: Blue_2 thumb 120×160 ×1, \"Denim Jacket / Blue\" $39.00, Discount code input + Apply, Subtotal $39.00 / Shipping $40.00 / Total $79.00 SemiBold; \"Create Account\" button→07.\n\nWait — \"Save This Information\" checkbox checked: checkbox component 10:2 now has Check VISIBLE by default (changed earlier!). So default instance = checked. For unchecked ones I hide Check (one-way, fine). For checked — default OK.\n\nField component 1:27: 420×87, children Label, Input, Placeholder. Placeholder override: set characters. Label override set label text. For two-col fields (First/Last name) resize to 480? Left col width: container 1400 → left col 880, right 440 at x=1220. Two-col: each 424 with gap 32.\n\nFields: instance 420×87; resize width → does text Input inside stretch? Input child likely a rect or text? Input is probably text node; resizing instance scales children? Instance resize: children with constraints scale. Might distort. In newsletter I used 400×87 instance — worked (Text Field instance 400×87). So resizing width is OK.\n\nCheckout layout:\n- header 96\n- \"FASCO Checkout\" Volkhov 44 @ (260,140)\n- left col x=260 w=880:\n  - \"Contact\" SemiBold 18 @ y=230; Email field @ y=266 (880 wide? resize 880 — too wide maybe fine) Actually keep fields 880 wide? In newsletter 400 wide fine. 880 wide fields look odd but checkout forms full width is normal. Use 880.\n  - \"Delivery\" SemiBold 18 @ y=390; country row: field-like box 880×56 @ y=426: text \"Country/Region\" sub + chevron right.\n  - First Name field (424) @ (260,502); Last Name @ (716,502).\n  - Address field 880 @ y=609.\n  - City field 424 @ (260,716); Postal Code @ (716,716).\n  - checkbox checked @ (260,830) + \"Save This Information\".\n  - \"Payment\" SemiBold 18 @ y=890; payment box: radio selected (circle 20 stroke ink + dot) + \"Credit Card\" + card icons? skip icons. @ y=926.\n  - Card Number field 880 @ y=966 — with Lock icon inside right: overlay icon 6:29 at field right.\n  - Expiration 424 @ (260,1073); Security Code 424 @ (716,1073).\n  - Card Holder 880 @ y=1180.\n  - checkbox checked @ (260,1294) + \"My billing address is the same as my delivery address\"? Brief: just \"checkbox\". Give \"Billing address is the same as delivery address\".\n  - Pay Now button 880×56 @ y=1330 — text \"Pay Now\".\n- right col x=1220 w=440: summary card surf radius 16, y=230, h≈640:\n  - \"Order Summary\" Volkhov Bold 24 @ (24,24)\n  - div y=80\n  - thumb 6:47 100×133 @ (24,100); \"Denim Jacket\" Medium 15 @ (140,104); \"Blue\" 13 sub @ (140,128); \"x 1\"? brief \"×1\". \"$39.00\" SemiBold @ right (416,104).\n  - div y=260\n  - Discount input: white box 392×48 @ (24,280) \"Discount code\" sub + Apply button? brief \"Discount code input + Apply\": box + Apply text button right — put Apply as small ink text button inside right.\n  - Subtotal row y=352: label sub, value right.\n  - Shipping row y=388: \"Shipping\" + \"$40.00\".\n  - div y=428\n  - Total row y=448: \"Total\" Medium 16 + \"$79.00\" SemiBold 18.\n  - \"Create Account\" button 392×56 @ (24,500) → 07.\n  Card height: 500+56+24=580. h=580.\n- content ends y=1330+56=1386. Footer @ y=1480? height 320 → frame 1800. Set footer (0,1480), frame height 1800.\n\nCheckbox checked = default now. Labels: \"Save This Information\", and payment checkbox \"Billing address is the same as delivery address\"? Hmm brief said just \"checkbox\" — I'll add reasonable label.\n\nField component placeholder override: find Placeholder node set characters; Label node set label. For Email field: Label \"Email Address\"? The brief: Contact (Email Address field). Set Label characters \"Email Address\", Placeholder \"your@email.com\"? Keep placeholder same as label? Simpler: Label = field name; Placeholder = example. For First Name: placeholder \"First name (and middle name if applicable)\"? Keep simple: \"First name\". \n\nField component structure: Label, Input, Placeholder. What is Input? Probably the input box rect. Fine.\n\nFont loading needed. Radio: ellipse 20 stroke ink 2 + inner dot ellipse 10 ink.\n\nWrite call for 06_Checkout.","signature":"6bfd7782d07f431982624e3c"}],"id":"c2a522dc-3f48-4cfb-bccc-6ae16b62da6b","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"115d8fd2-329d-45e7-8005-49ec3e8a31e3","uuid":"5709fdcf-eaf1-415f-b8b1-9dbf61e94c2b","timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:34:18.230Z","thinking_duration_ms":27013}
