{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The error message reveals the new reactions schema. Key line:\n\n\"Multiple issues at [0].action:\n  Required value missing at [0].action.navigation\n  Expected [0].action.transition ...\"\n\nSo the NODE action now has shape: `{type:\"NODE\", navigation: {...}, transition: {...}}`. The `navigation` value — probably `{type:\"NAVIGATE\", destinationId:\"...\"}` or similar. The error says for action.type enum: 'BACK' | 'CLOSE' received 'NODE'... wait that's one variant: `{type:'BACK'|'CLOSE'}` no navigation. Another variant: `{type:\"NODE\", navigation: <required>, transition: <required>}`. Hmm — action type \"NODE\" is invalid?? \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE'\" — that suggests in this schema version, navigate actions are typed differently. Let me think: newer Figma plugin API introduced `NavigationAction`? Actually the modern schema for prototyping actions in the Plugin API:\n\n```ts\ninterface NavigateAction {\n  type: \"NODE\"\n  destinationId: string\n  navigationType: \"NAVIGATE\" | \"SWAP\" | \"OVERLAY\"...\n}\n```\nThat's the OLD one. The error says that shape is unrecognized and instead expects `action.navigation` + `action.transition`. This matches the NEW prototyping schema (2024+): \n- Action types: \"CONDITIONAL\" | \"BACK\" | \"CLOSE\" | \"URL\" | \"UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME\" | \"NODE\"?? \n\nHmm the enum says 'BACK' | 'CLOSE' for one variant, 'URL' for another... and the failing variant with navigation/transition didn't report a type literal error — meaning `type:\"NODE\"` WAS accepted for that variant! Look: the variant \"Required value missing at [0].action.navigation / Expected transition...\" has NO \"Invalid literal value ... received 'NODE'\" complaint and no complaint about destinationId being unrecognized... wait it does complain \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'navigationType'\" in attempt A (because navigationType isn't part of schema) but NOT about destinationId?? In attempt A: variant lists \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'navigationType'\" — destinationId not listed as unrecognized → destinationId IS a valid key of that variant. And navigation is required.\n\nSo the correct shape: `{type:\"NODE\", destinationId:\"24:278\", navigation:\"NAVIGATE\"?, transition:{...}}`. Hmm navigation value type unknown. Possibly `navigation: \"NAVIGATE\" | \"SWAP\" | \"OVERLAY\" | \"SCROLL_TO\"`. And transition required: e.g. `{type:\"INSTANT\"}` or `{type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration:0.3}`.\n\nTrigger ON_CLICK is valid (error C complained about 'CLICK' but ON_CLICK accepted — in attempts A/B trigger didn't error? Actually error A ends with \"Expected [0].trigger to be one of the following...\" — that's from attempt C (trigger CLICK). In A and B, trigger ON_CLICK didn't appear in errors... the error text for A covers only action issues, then B covers action, C covers action + trigger. So ON_CLICK is fine.\n\nTry: `btn.reactions=[{action:{type:\"NODE\",destinationId:\"24:278\",navigation:\"NAVIGATE\",transition:{type:\"INSTANT\"}},trigger:{type:\"ON_CLICK\"}}]`. If navigation enum wrong, error will tell. Maybe transition INSTANT invalid; alternatives: {type:\"DISSOLVE\",duration:0.2,easing:...}. Let me probe variants quickly on the same button, trying a few shapes and capturing only first error line (truncate message to 300 chars).","signature":"44e171367bef4f1fa4ae49b3"}],"id":"7664f9d5-254e-4dbb-8767-e30e5bf59794","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"115d8fd2-329d-45e7-8005-49ec3e8a31e3","uuid":"53875425-b4d8-4d74-8a8f-e046d3daf693","timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:38:50.945Z","thinking_duration_ms":15648}
